The equation $y=-16t^2+22t+45$ can be rewritten as $y=(8t+9)(-2t+5)$. Because $t$ needs to be positive, set $-2t+5=0$ to represent the point where the ball reaches the ground. Therefore: \begin{align*}
-2t+5&=0\\
-2t&=-5\\
2t&=5\\
t&=\boxed{\frac{5}{2}}
\end{align*}

This 4-term geometric series has first term $a_0 = \frac13$ and ratio $r=\frac13$, so it has value  \begin{align*}
\dfrac{\dfrac13\left(1-\left(\dfrac13\right)^{4}\right)}{1-\frac13} &= \dfrac{\dfrac13(1-\left(\dfrac13\right)^{4})}{\dfrac23}\\
&=\dfrac12\left(1-\left(\dfrac13\right)^{4}\right)\\
&=\dfrac12\left(\dfrac{80}{81}\right)\\
&=\boxed{\dfrac{40}{81}}.
\end{align*}

The common factor of 3 in the numerator and the common factor of 3 in the denominator will cancel: \[
\frac{3^4+3^2}{3^3-3}=\frac{3(3^3+3^1)}{3(3^2-1)}=\frac{3^3+3^1}{3^2-1}
\] Now the numerator is $3^3+3=27+3=30$, and the denominator is $3^2-1=9-1=8$.  Therefore, the fraction simplifies to $\dfrac{30}{8}=\boxed{\dfrac{15}{4}}$.

Since $8=\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{-3}$ the equation can be rewritten as $\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{-3(4x-6)}=\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{x+5}$. From this equation, we see that $-3(4x-6)=x+5$. Simplifying we get, \begin{align*}
-12x+18&=x+5\\
\Rightarrow -13x+18&=5\\
\Rightarrow -13x&=-13\\
\Rightarrow x&=\boxed{1}.
\end{align*}
